{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Missing Postgres Service Container in CircleCI",
    "Explanation": [
      "The job's only Docker image is circleci/node, and no PostgreSQL service container is defined in the `docker:` section. The dockerize step installed correctly, since the binary ran and produced output. It then polled localhost:5432 and got 'connection refused' every time for the full minute. That means nothing was listening on the port at all; the database was not simply slow to start.",
      "",
      "In CircleCI, every image listed after the first under `docker:` runs as a service container. Service containers share the primary container's network, so they are reachable on localhost.",
      "",
      "The fix is to add a Postgres image as a secondary image, for example:",
      "",
      "```yaml",
      "docker:",
      "  - image: circleci/node",
      "  - image: circleci/postgres:9.6-alpine",
      "    environment:",
      "      POSTGRES_USER: root",
      "      POSTGRES_DB: circle_test",
      "```",
      "",
      "With this in place, dockerize will find the database on localhost:5432 and the job will go green. Changing the timeout, host or port would not help, because no database exists to connect to."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"fix\": \"add_postgres_service_image\",",
      "  \"root_cause\": \"no_postgres_service_container\"",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"fix\": \"add_postgres_service_image\",",
        "  \"root_cause\": \"no_postgres_service_container\"",
        "}"
      ]
    ],
    "Usage": {
      "InputTokens": 2173,
      "OutputTokens": 416
    }
  },
