{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Missing Ruby Orb Install Step",
    "Explanation": [
      "The log shows 'ruby: command not found' (exit code 127), which means `ruby -v` ran on the plain `cimg/base:stable` image. The config has only placeholder comments where the orb and install step should go, so no Ruby install was ever attempted. The requirement is to use the `circleci/ruby` orb. The fix is to declare the orb and add an install step before `ruby -v`:",
      "",
      "```yaml",
      "orbs:",
      "  ruby: circleci/ruby@x.y.z",
      "```",
      "",
      "and, after `checkout`:",
      "",
      "```yaml",
      "- ruby/install:",
      "    version: '2.6.3'",
      "```",
      "",
      "Replace `x.y.z` with an actual version of the orb."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"fix\": \"add_ruby_orb\",",
      "  \"install_attempted\": false",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"fix\": \"add_ruby_orb\",",
        "  \"install_attempted\": false",
        "}"
      ]
    ],
    "Usage": {
      "InputTokens": 995,
      "OutputTokens": 294
    }
  },
