{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Enable Yarn cache keyed on package.json",
    "Explanation": [
      "The build failed because `yarn install --offline` needs packages already in the local Yarn cache (`~/.cache/yarn`). The log shows no cache was restored, since the `restore_cache` step is commented out. The cache was empty (\"possible versions are \\\"\\\"\"), so Yarn could not resolve left-pad@1.3.0. The log also shows \"info No lockfile found\", so there is no yarn.lock to checksum. That matches the requirement to cache based on `package.json`.",
      "",
      "Because `--offline` cannot be removed, both cache steps must be enabled:",
      "1. `restore_cache` before the install step, with keys such as `v1-yarn-packages-{{ checksum \"package.json\" }}`, plus an optional fallback such as `v1-yarn-packages-`.",
      "2. `save_cache` after the install step, with key `v1-yarn-packages-{{ checksum \"package.json\" }}` and paths `~/.cache/yarn`.",
      "",
      "Using only one step does not work. Restore alone never fills the cache. Save alone never feeds later builds.",
      "",
      "Note: with the `--offline` flag fixed, the very first run still has nothing to restore. `save_cache` only runs if the install succeeds, so something has to put packages into `~/.cache/yarn` once before the first save. Examples are a one-time online install or seeding the cache another way. After that, later builds can restore it.",
      "",
      "Forcing a new cache save: CircleCI caches are immutable, and an existing key is never overwritten. To force a fresh save, change the key. For example, bump the version prefix from `v1-` to `v2-` in both the restore and save keys. Changing `package.json` also changes the checksum and produces a new key automatically."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"cache_restored\": false,",
      "  \"checksum_target\": \"package.json\",",
      "  \"fix\": \"enable_restore_and_save_cache\"",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"cache_restored\": false,",
        "  \"checksum_target\": \"package.json\",",
        "  \"fix\": \"enable_restore_and_save_cache\"",
        "}"
      ]
    ],
    "Usage": {
      "InputTokens": 1427,
      "OutputTokens": 861
    }
  },
