{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Deploy runs on non-production branch",
    "Explanation": [
      "The pipeline (#151) is green: build, test-production and deploy all succeeded. However, it ran on branch `koans-08-branch-filters`, not `production`, and the deploy job still executed. The workflow has no branch filter, so every branch triggers deploy, which violates the requirement that deploy only runs on commits to `production`. A green pipeline therefore does not mean the requirement is met. The `requires` keys only enforce ordering (build → test-production → deploy); they do not restrict which branches a job runs on. The fix is to add a `filters.branches.only: production` block to the `deploy` job entry in the workflow, not to the job definition under `jobs:`. build and test-production can continue running on every branch:",
      "",
      "```yaml",
      "- deploy:",
      "    requires:",
      "      - test-production",
      "    filters:",
      "      branches:",
      "        only: production",
      "```",
      "",
      "An `ignore` list would require naming every non-production branch, which is fragile. `only: production` expresses the requirement directly."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"filters_branches_only_production\",",
      "  \"fix_target_job\": \"deploy\",",
      "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
        "  \"fix\": \"filters_branches_only_production\",",
        "  \"fix_target_job\": \"deploy\",",
        "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
        "}"
      ]
    ],
    "Usage": {
      "InputTokens": 1393,
      "OutputTokens": 409
    }
