{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Deploy fails because app files were never persisted",
    "Explanation": [
      "The workflow summary shows that build-linux, build-mac and build-windows all succeeded. Only the deploy job failed.",
      "",
      "The cause is in what each build job saves. Each one runs persist_to_workspace with a root of '.', but the paths list only its metadata directory (meta/linux, meta/windows or meta/mac). The app/\u003cplatform\u003e directories that hold the generated app files are never added to the workspace.",
      "",
      "The deploy log confirms this. After attach_workspace, the only files present are ./meta/linux/build.txt, ./meta/mac/build.txt and ./meta/windows/build.txt. The step `test -f app/linux/app.linux` therefore fails with exit code 1, and deploy fails before store_artifacts runs.",
      "",
      "The fix is to add app/\u003cplatform\u003e to the persist_to_workspace paths in each build job (for example, paths: [meta/linux, app/linux]). With the apps persisted, attach_workspace at '.' will restore app/linux, app/windows and app/mac, the verification step will pass, and store_artifacts will upload the app directory.",
      "",
      "The other options would not work:",
      "- Storing artifacts in the build jobs does not deliver the files to deploy.",
      "- Fixing only one platform leaves the other two tests failing.",
      "- Changing only attach_workspace cannot restore files that were never persisted.",
      "- Removing only the verification step would hide the problem and upload no apps."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"builds_green\": true,",
      "  \"deploy_green\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"persist_app_paths\",",
      "  \"workspace_had_apps\": false",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"builds_green\": true,",
        "  \"deploy_green\": false,",
        "  \"fix\": \"persist_app_paths\",",
        "  \"workspace_had_apps\": false",
        "}"
      ]
    ],
